    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nThe `-` mapping from a `:terminal` buffer goes to nonsense.\n\nSteps:\n\n1. run `:te`, then the buffername is `term://~/foo//82225:/bin/bash`\n2. hit `-`\n3. dir.lua navigates to `~/foo/term:/~/foo/82140:/bin`\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`-` should do something reasonable on non-file buffers, presumably it should go to the buffer's effective CWD (`getcwd()`)\n\ncc @barrettruth ",
    "closed_at": "2026-07-28T17:37:08Z",
